  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If \\(\\log_MN=\\log_NM,\\) \\(M\\ne N,\\) \\(MN\\gt0,\\) and \\(M\\ne1,\\) \\(N\\ne1,\\) then \\(MN\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac12\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "a number greater than \\(2\\) and less than \\(10\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "1"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1966-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Change of base gives \\[ \\frac{\\ln N}{\\ln M}=\\frac{\\ln M}{\\ln N}, \\] so \\((\\ln M)^2=(\\ln N)^2.\\) Equality of the logs themselves would give \\(M=N,\\) which is excluded. Hence \\(\\ln M=-\\ln N,\\) and \\(\\ln(MN)=0.\\) Thus \\(MN=1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write both logarithms using natural logs",
        "The equality gives \\((\\ln M)^2=(\\ln N)^2\\); use \\(M\\ne N\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
